<section class="site-wrap faq-section"><div class="section-intro"><p class="kicker">NO GUESSWORK</p><h2>A few things<br>worth knowing.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details open><summary>What does one credit buy?</summary><p>Credits are Sahdev usage units. Each model has published input and output rates per million tokens. A reply’s cost depends on the model and actual tokens used. Rates appear in your brand workspace; a pack does not promise a fixed number of replies.</p></details><details><summary>Are these subscriptions?</summary><p>No. These are one-time prepaid packs with no automatic renewal. HostingSpell issues an invoice. Credits become available after payment is verified. Existing orders keep the price shown when they were created.</p></details><details><summary>How do pooled and allocated credits differ?</summary><p>A pooled brand uses the organization balance, subject to its monthly budget. An allocated brand can only use the credits assigned to it. Moving credits between the pool and a brand does not create extra credits.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when a request fails?</summary><p>A confirmed rejection releases its reserved credits. If the provider’s outcome is unknown, the hold stays open for review so a retry does not silently create another charge.</p></details><details><summary>Does a budget renew my credits?</summary><p>No. A monthly budget is a spending cap, not a purchase. Budget periods use UTC calendar months. You top up the balance separately.</p></details><details><summary>Which features are ready to test?</summary><p>The current thin connector previews ticket analysis, summaries, rewrites, quality scoring and canned drafts. Other standard-module features are still being migrated. Check the <a href="/installation#preview">release scope</a> before installing.</p></details></div></section>
